   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:53,713:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: viii — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:53,714:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="page-break-after: always;"></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:53,714:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ABSTRACT
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:53,760:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The proliferation of misinformation on digital platforms has emerged as one of the most pressing challenges in
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:53,792:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: contemporary information dissemination. Existing social media systems predominantly rely on engagement-driven
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:53,812:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: metrics — likes, shares, and view counts — to determine content visibility, which inadvertently amplifies sensational and
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:53,828:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: often misleading content without any systematic verification. This problem is especially acute in the domain of local
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:53,831:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: news, where communities require timely, reliable information about events happening in their immediate vicinity
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:53,832:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: but lack the institutional infrastructure that major news outlets possess for fact-checking.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:53,833:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: This project presents the 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:53,833:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Network-aware Credibility and Propagation System (NCPS)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:53,938:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: , a full-stack web platform
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,037:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: that fundamentally replaces engagement-driven content distribution with a credibility-driven approach. The system
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,116:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: treats each user as a noisy sensor and employes Bayesian inference to estimate post credibility from weighted
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,176:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: community votes, where user weights themselves are derived from a multi-dimensional trust assessment. The core
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,220:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: architecture comprises six interconnected computation engines: (1) a User Engine that maintains Bayesian reliability
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,248:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: estimates with confidence correction, (2) a Post Engine that computes credibility through weighted evidence
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,267:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: aggregation, (3) a Graph Engine that propagates trust through social networks while detecting coordinated
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,277:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: manipulation, (4) a Spatial Engine that incorporates location-based trust signals and controls geographic
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,282:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: propagation, (5) an ML Engine providing machine learning augmentation with memory-based similarity scoring,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,282:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: and (6) a Decision Engine that integrates all signals through a conservative 5-condition gate for propagation control.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,325:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The system was developed iteratively over six phases, progressively adding capabilities from basic Bayesian
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,355:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: estimation (Phase 1) through graph trust propagation (Phase 3), anomaly detection (Phase 4), ML augmentation
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,375:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: (Phase 5), to extended spatial and behavioral signals (Phase 6). Simulation results demonstrate that the final system
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,385:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: achieves perfect accuracy (1.000) with zero attack success rate across diverse adversarial scenarios, including
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,389:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: coordinated bot attacks and location spoofing. The platform is implemented using FastAPI (backend), React and
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,389:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: vanilla JavaScript (frontend), PostgreSQL (database), with a comprehensive simulation framework for empirical
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,390:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: validation.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,390:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Keywords
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,393:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Misinformation detection, Bayesian credibility estimation, trust propagation, anomaly detection, local
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,393:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: news verification, graph-based coordination detection, spatial trust
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,394:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ix — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,395:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="page-break-after: always;"></div>
