   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,595:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: xviii — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,596:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="page-break-after: always;"></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,597:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CHAPTER 1
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,597:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: INTRODUCTION
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,598:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1.1 Overview
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,635:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The last decade has witnessed a dramatic transformation in how information is consumed and shared across society.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,661:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: With the rise of social media platforms and user-generated content, traditional gatekeeping mechanisms that once
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,675:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: governed news dissemination have largely been bypassed. While this democratization of information has undeniable
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,682:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: benefits — giving voice to marginalized communities, enabling citizen journalism, and facilitating rapid information
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,683:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: sharing during emergencies — it has also created fertile ground for the spread of misinformation and disinformation at
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,684:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: unprecedented scales.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,708:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The World Economic Forum has consistently ranked digital misinformation among the top global risks, and for
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,722:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: good reason. During events ranging from natural disasters to public health crises, the inability to quickly distinguish
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,728:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: reliable information from fabricated or misleading content has had tangible, sometimes tragic consequences. People
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,730:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: have made harmful decisions based on unverified social media posts, and the sheer volume of information makes
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,730:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: manual verification practically impossible.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,766:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: What makes this problem particulary challenging is that existing platforms are fundamentally not designed to
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,789:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: address it. The dominant social media architectures — Facebook, Twitter (now X), Instagram, and others — are built
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,801:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: around engagement maximization. Content that generates more clicks, shares, and reactions gets amplified,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,805:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: regardless of its factual accuracy. In fact, research has shown that false information tends to spread faster and farther
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,806:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: than true information precisely because it tends to be more novel and emotionally provocative 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,806:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,807:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,807:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,809:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . This creates a
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,809:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: perverse incentive structure where the most misleading content often recieves the widest distribution.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,810:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: This project is motivated by a simple but powerful question: 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,811:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: what if content distribution was governed not by
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,811:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: engagement metrics, but by credibility assessment?
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,820:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  Rather than amplifying whatever gets the most clicks, what if
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,824:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: we could build a system that evaluates the likely truthfulness of user-submitted reports and adjusts their visibility
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,824:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: accordingly? This is the foundational idea behind the Network-aware Credibility and Propagation System (NCPS).
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,825:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,826:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1.1.1 The Misinformation Crisis in Digital Media
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,837:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The scale of the misinformation problem is staggering. According to a landmark study published in Science by
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,841:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Vosoughi, Roy, and Aral (2018), false news stories on Twitter were 70% more likely to be retweeted than true
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,842:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: stories, and they reached their first 1,500 people approximately six times faster 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,842:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,843:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,843:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,845:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . This asymmetry is not a bug in
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,845:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: the system — it is a direct consequence of how engagement-driven algorithms operate.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,846:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Several factors contribute to the rapid spread of misinformation in digital ecosystems:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,846:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1. Algorithmic Amplification
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,855:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Social media algorithms are designed to maximize user engagement. Content that
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,860:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: provokes strong emotional reactions — outrage, fear, surprise — naturally generates more interaction. Unfortunately,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,861:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: fabricated or sensationalized content often triggers these emotions more effectively than nuanced, factual reporting.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,861:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2. Information Overload
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,874:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : The sheer volume of content produced daily makes it impossible for users to individually
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,880:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: verify every piece of information they encounter. Studies have shown that the average person encounters dozens of
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,881:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: potentially misleading posts per day, yet invests only a few seconds deciding whether to engage with or share each
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,882:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: one 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,882:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,883:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,883:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,883:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: .
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,884:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3. Echo Chambers and Filter Bubbles
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,894:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Algorithmic personalization tends to show users content that aligns with
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,900:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: their existing beliefs, making it harder for corrective information to reach those who have already been exposed to
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,901:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: misinformation. Once a false narrative takes hold within a community, it can be extremly difficult to dislodge.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,901:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 4. Coordinated Inauthentic Behavior
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,910:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Perhaps most concerning is the rise of organized disinformation campaigns,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,915:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: where networks of bot accounts and paid actors deliberately spread false narratives. These coordinated attacks
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,915:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: exploit the open nature of social media platforms and are increasingly sophisticated in their tactics.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,916:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 5. Local News Vacuum
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,924:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : The decline of local journalism has left many communities without reliable sources of
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,927:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: information about events in their immediate vicinity. This vacuum is increasingly being filled by unverified social
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,928:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: media posts and community groups, where misinformation can spread unchecked.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,929:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The problem is not just academic. During the COVID-19 pandemic, the World Health Organization coined the term 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,929:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,930:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: infodemic
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,930:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,950:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  to describe the flood of misinformation that accompanied the health crisis. False claims about
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,961:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: treatments, vaccine safety, and the origins of the virus spread rapidly through social media, contributing to vaccine
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,966:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: hesitancy and the adoption of unproven remedies. In India specifically, WhatsApp-forwarded misinformation has
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,967:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: been linked to mob violence incidents, highlighting the very real consequences of unchecked information spread 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,967:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,968:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,968:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,969:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: .
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,970:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,971:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1.1.2 Engagement-Driven vs. Credibility-Driven Systems
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,972:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: To understand the motivation behind NCPS, it is essential to contrasts two fundamentally different approaches to
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,972:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: content distribution.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,973:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Engagement-Driven Systems (Current Paradigm)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:54,999:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: In an engagement-driven system, the visibility of content is determined primarily by how much interaction it
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,014:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: generates. When a user posts something, the platform tracks metrics like likes, shares, comments, and time spent
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,019:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: viewing. Content that scores high on these engagement metrics gets pushed to more users feeds, creating a positive
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,020:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: feedback loop. The more people see it, the more engagement it generates, and the more the algorithm promotes it.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,044:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The fundamental problem here is that engagement and truthfulness are not correlated. A fabricated story about a
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,057:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: local politician might generate enormous engagement due to its shocking nature, while a carefully fact-checked
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,063:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: correction of that story might generate relatively little interest. The engagement-driven algorithm would amplify the
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,064:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: former and bury the latter, which is exactly the opposite of what a healthy information ecosystem requires.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,064:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Credibility-Driven Systems (NCPS Approach)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,075:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The NCPS takes a fundamentally different approach. Instead of measuring engagement, it measures credibility.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,080:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: When a user submits a report (for example, about a local event like a road accident or water supply disruption), the
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,080:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: system does not simply count how many people interact with it. Instead, it:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,081:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  1 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,081:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Treats each user as a noisy sensor
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,082:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  with an estimated reliability score, rather then treating all users
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,082:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: equally
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,082:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,083:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Computes Bayesian credibility estimates
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,083:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  for each post based on weighted votes from the
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,084:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: community
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,084:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,085:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Detects anomalous behavior
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,085:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  such as coordinated voting, location spoofing, and burst activity
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,086:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: patterns
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,086:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  4 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,087:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Propagates trust through the social graph
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,087:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  to leverage network structure for credibility assessment
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,087:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  5 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,088:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Controls geographic propagation
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,089:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  — only expanding the reach of posts that meet stringent credibility
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,089:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: thresholds
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,100:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: This approach ensures that the system is inherently resistant to manipulation. Even if a large group of bot accounts
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,104:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: tries to upvote a false report, their votes are automatically down-weighted because the system detects their
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,105:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: coordinated behavior, flags their anomalous patterns, and reduces their trust scores through graph-based
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,106:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: propagation.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,106:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The following figure illustrates the key difference between these two paradigms:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,109:      pdf_renderer.py:  235: /Users/chandraprakash/.gemini/antigravity/brain/608c58f2-8d2c-4b04-972b-ca1c9279e9d7/fig_1_1_engagement_vs_credibility_1780257502565.png, 1024, 1024
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,112:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Fig 1.1: Comparison of Engagement-Driven vs. Credibility-Driven News Dissemination Systems
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,134:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: As shown in Fig 1.1, the engagement-driven system on the left allows misinformation to spread unchecked because
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,146:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: popularity metrics do not distinguish between true and false content. In contrast, the credibility-driven system on the
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,151:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: right incorporates trust scoring, Bayesian credibility assessment, and anomaly detection to ensure only verified
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,152:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: content recieves wider propagation. This is the core architectural difference that motivates the entire NCPS design.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,153:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 4 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,153:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1.2 Motivation
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,156:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The motivation for this project stems from several converging factors that make the development of a
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,157:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: credibility-driven news verification system both timely and necessary.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,157:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The Local News Gap
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,165:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : While major news events are typically covered by established media organizations with
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,169:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: editorial standards and fact-checking processes, local news suffers from a significant coverage gap. Newsroom
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,169:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: employment in the United States dropped by 26% between 2008 and 2020 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,170:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,170:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 4
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,170:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,184:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: , and similar trends are observed in
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,194:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: India, where many districts have virtually no professional journalists. Community events — accidents, infrastructure
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,197:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: failures, public safety incidents — are increasingly reported first (and sometimes only) through social media and
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,198:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: messaging apps. These reports, however, come with no guarantee of accuracy.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,198:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Inadequacy of Existing Solutions
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,200:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Current approaches to misinformation detection, while valuable, have
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,200:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: significant limitations for the local news domain:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,200:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,201:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Manual fact-checking
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,203:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  is too slow for time-sensitive local events. By the time a fact-checker
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,204:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: reviews a report, the damage may already be done.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,204:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,204:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Content-based ML approaches
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,206:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (analyzing text, images, or videos for signs of fabrication) require
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,206:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: large training datasets that don
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,206:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,207:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t exist for local news contexts, and they struggle with novel events
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,208:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: that don
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,208:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,208:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t match training patterns.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,209:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,209:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Platform-level interventions
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,210:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (like Twitter
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,210:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,210:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s community notes or Facebook
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,211:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,212:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s fact-checking
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,212:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: partnerships) are designed for viral content and don
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,212:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,214:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t scale down to hyper-local reports that may
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,214:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: only be relevant to a few hundred people.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,214:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The Trust Problem
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,255:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Perhaps most fundamentally, existing systems treat all users equally. A post from a first-time
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,285:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: anonymous account is given the same initial visibility as one from a long-established community member with a
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,304:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: track record of accurate reporting. This egalitarian approach, while well-intentioned, creates obvious vulnerabilities.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,314:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The NCPS addresses this by maintaining fine-grained trust profiles for every user, incorporating their historical
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,317:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: reliability, their position in the social network, their geographic consistency, and their behavioral patterns into a
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,318:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: comprehensive weight that determines the influence of their votes and reports.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,318:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Geographic Relevance
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,323:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Local news is, by definition, geographically bounded. A report about a traffic accident in
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,324:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: South Delhi is highly relevant to people in that area but largely irrelevant to someone in Mumbai. Existing platforms
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,325:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: don
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,325:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,332:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t incorporate this spatial dimension into content distribution in any meaningful way. The NCPS introduces
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,333:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: spatial-aware propagation, where the geographic reach of a report expands only as its credibility increases, ensuring
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,334:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: that unverified claims don
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,334:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,335:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t unnecessarily alarm distant communities.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,335:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Conservative Design Philosophy
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,360:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : The NCPS embodies a deliberatly conservative design philosophy. In
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,376:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: information systems, the cost of amplifying false information typically far exceeds the cost of slightly delaying the
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,382:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: spread of true information. Therefore, the system is designed so that trust can only decrease through manipulation — it
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,384:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: can never be artificially inflated. This asymmetry is a conscious design choice that makes the system fundamentally
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,384:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: resistant to gaming.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,385:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 5 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,386:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1.3 Problem Statement
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,387:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Given a stream of user-generated local news reports and community votes on those reports, the problem is to:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,388:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  1 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,388:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Estimate the credibility
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,392:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  of each report in near-real-time, based on the weighted opinions of
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,393:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: community members whose individual reliabilities are themselves uncertain and must be estimated
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,393:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: simultaneously.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,394:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,394:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Detect and mitigate manipulation attempts
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,396:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  including coordinated bot attacks, location spoofing,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,397:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: and adversarial voting strategies, without requiring manual moderation.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,397:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,398:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Control the geographic propagation
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,401:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  of reports such that only sufficiently credible content is
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,402:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: allowed to spread beyond its immediate locality, preventing unverified claims from reaching distant
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,402:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: communities.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,403:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Formally, the problem can be stated as follows:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,405:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Given a set of users U = {u₁, u₂, ..., uₙ}, a set of posts P = {p₁, p₂, ..., pₘ}, and a set of interactions I = {(uᵢ, pⱼ, vᵢⱼ)} where vᵢⱼ ∈ {-1,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,414:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: +1} represents user uᵢ
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,414:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,414:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s vote on post pⱼ, compute:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,414:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,415:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: User weights
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,417:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  w = {w₁, w₂, ..., wₙ} where each wᵢ reflects the estimated trustworthiness of user uᵢ,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,418:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: incorporating reliability, experience, anomaly detection, and graph-based trust propagation.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,418:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,418:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Post credibilities
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,420:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  C = {C₁, C₂, ..., Cₘ} where each Cⱼ represents the estimated truthfulness of post pⱼ,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,420:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: derived from Bayesian aggregation of weighted votes.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,421:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,421:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Propagation decisions
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,423:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  D = {d₁, d₂, ..., dₘ} where each dⱼ determines whether post pⱼ should be allowed to
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,424:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: expand its geographic reach based on a multi-criteria assessment.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,447:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The key challenge is the circular dependency between user weights and post credibilities: to compute accurate
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,460:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: credibility for a post, we need reliable user weights, but to assess user reliability, we need to know the true
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,465:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: credibility of posts they voted on. The NCPS resolves this chicken-and-egg problem through iterative Bayesian
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,467:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: estimation with conservative priors, augmented by independent signals (graph structure, spatial behavior, temporal
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,467:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: patterns) that break the circularity.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,468:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 6 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,469:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1.4 Objectives
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,472:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The primary objective of this project is to design, implement, and evaluate a comprehensive credibility-driven
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,473:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: content distribution system for local news verification. Specific objectives include:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,473:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  1 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,474:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Design a Bayesian credibility estimation framework
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,477:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  that treats users as noisy sensors with
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,478:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: uncertain reliabilities and computes posterior credibility scores for user-submitted reports,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,479:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: incorporating confidence-corrected user weights.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,479:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,480:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Develop a multi-dimensional user trust model
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,480:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  that goes beyond simple reputation scores by
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,481:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: incorporating:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,481:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,482:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Bayesian reliability estimation with confidence correction
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,482:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,483:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Experience-weighted contribution (logarithmic scaling)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,483:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,484:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Multi-signal anomaly detection (burst, entropy, consensus, coordination, location)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,484:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,484:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Graph-based trust propagation with safety constraints
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,485:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,485:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Implement graph-based coordination detection
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,487:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  to identify clusters of users engaging in
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,488:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: coordinated manipulation, using agreement-frequency-temporal similarity features and link
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,489:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: dampening.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,489:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  4 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,489:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Design a spatial trust subsystem
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,493:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  that leverages geographic information for both user verification
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,494:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: (location consistency, device/IP patterns) and content propagation control (radius expansion
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,495:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: governed by credibility thresholds).
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,495:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  5 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,496:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Integrate machine learning augmentation
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,498:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  to supplement Bayesian estimation with learned
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,499:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: patterns, including a memory module that detects textual similarity with historically resolved
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,500:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: reports.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,500:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  6 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,501:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Build a conservative propagation decision engine
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,503:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  that uses a 5-condition AND gate to ensure only
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,503:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: sufficiently verified content is allowed to expand its geographic reach.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,504:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  7 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,504:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Develop a full-stack web application
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,508:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  with a React-based frontend, FastAPI backend, PostgreSQL
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,509:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: database, and comprehensive REST API that demonstrates all system capabilities through an
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,510:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: intuitive user interface.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,510:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  8 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,511:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Create a simulation framework
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,517:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  for empirical validation that models diverse user populations
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,520:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: (honest, noisy, adversarial, coordinated bots) and measures system performance across multiple
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,521:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: metrics including accuracy, attack success rate, Brier score, and weight correlation.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,521:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1.5 Scope and Limitations
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,522:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Scope
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,528:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : The system is designed as a proof-of-concept platform demonstrating credibility-driven content distribution
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,529:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: for local news. It handles text-based news reports, community voting, geographic visualization, and trust
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,530:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: computation. The current scope includes:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,530:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,530:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Full user authentication and authorization
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,531:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,531:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Report creation with geographic tagging
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,531:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,532:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Community voting with credibility feedback
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,532:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,533:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Interactive map-based visualization
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,533:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,533:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Trust profile display and decomposition
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,534:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,534:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Simulation-based validation with configurable scenarios
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,535:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Limitations
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,535:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : The current implementation has several known limitations:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,535:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,537:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The system does not perform content analysis (NLP-based fake news detection on text/images) — it
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,537:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: relies entirely on network-based signals
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,538:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,538:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Real-world deployment would require integration with external verification sources
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,539:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,539:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The simulation uses synthetic data; real-world user behavior may differ significantly from simulated
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,540:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: patterns
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,540:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,541:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The current system supports single-language (English) content only
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,541:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,542:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Location services depend on browser-provided geolocation, which users can spoof at the browser
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,542:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: level
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,543:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 8 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,544:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1.6 Organization of Report
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,545:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The remainder of this report is organized as follows:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,545:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Chapter 2: Literature Survey
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,563:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  provides a comprehensive review of existing work in misinformation detection,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,574:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: including content-based approaches, source credibility assessment, propagation-based detection, truth discovery,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,579:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: crowdsourced verification, location-aware information systems, and trust propagation in networks. Each approach is
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,580:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: analyzed for its strengths and limitations, identifying the gaps that NCPS aims to address.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,580:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Chapter 3: Proposed Methodology
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,589:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  presents the complete technical design of the NCPS, including the system
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,593:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: architecture, all six computation engines, the mathematical formulation of all 13 key formulas, the 14 input signals,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,594:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: the algorithms used, the phased development approach, and the technology stack.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,594:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Chapter 4: Results and Discussion
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,603:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  presents the experimental evaluation of the system across all six development
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,607:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: phases, including quantitative metrics (accuracy, attack success rate, Brier score, weight correlation, anomaly
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,608:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: precision and recall), frontend implementation screenshots, functional test results, and stress test scenarios.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,609:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Chapter 5: Conclusion and Future Works
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,612:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  summarizes the contributions of this project, presents key findings
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,612:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: from the experimental evaluation, and outlines directions for future research and development.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,614:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The report concludes with references and three appendices containing the complete API endpoint reference,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,615:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: hyperparameter reference table, and setup/execution guide.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,616:      pdf_renderer.py:  235: /Users/chandraprakash/.gemini/antigravity/brain/608c58f2-8d2c-4b04-972b-ca1c9279e9d7/fig_3_1_ncps_architecture_1780257517758.png, 1024, 1024
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,621:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Fig 1.2: General NCPS Architecture Overview showing the layered design with Client Layer, API Gateway, six
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,621:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: computation engines, and data stores
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,622:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 9 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,623:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="page-break-after: always;"></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,623:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <!-- Blank page -->
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,624:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 10 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,624:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="page-break-after: always;"></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,625:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CHAPTER 2
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,625:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: LITERATURE SURVEY
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,643:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The problem of misinformation detection and credibility assessment has attracted significant attention from the
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,652:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: research community over the past decade. This chapter provides a comprehensive review of existing approaches,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,655:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: organized by their primary methodology. For each approach, we examine the underlying technique, its strengths,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,656:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: and crucially, the limitations that motivate the design choices in NCPS.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,656:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2.1 Content-Based Fake News Detection
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,660:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Content-based approaches attempt to determine the veracity of information by analyzing the content itself — the text,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,661:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: images, or structural features of a news article or social media post.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,661:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1. Deep Learning for Fake News Detection (Ruchansky et al., 2017)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,671:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Ruchansky, Diaz, and Wang proposed CSI (Capture, Score, and Integrate), a hybrid deep learning model that
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,674:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: combines an LSTM-based module for capturing temporal patterns in user engagement, a source credibility scoring
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,675:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: module, and an integration module that produces a final fake/true classification 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,675:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,675:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 5
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,676:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,691:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . The model was evaluated on
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,703:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Twitter and Weibo datasets and achieved around 95% accuracy. However, the approach requires large labeled
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,707:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: training datasets and operates as a post-hoc classifier — it can only assess content after it has already spread, making it
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,708:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: unsuitable for real-time credibility estimation during the early stages of information propagation.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,708:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2. Geometric Deep Learning for Social Media (Monti et al., 2019)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,711:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Monti et al. explored the use of graph convolutional networks (GCNs) for fake news detection, leveraging the
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,711:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: geometric structure of user interaction patterns 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,711:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,712:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 6
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,712:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,740:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . By treating the problem as a graph classification task where
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,762:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: nodes represent users and edges represent sharing/commenting relationships, they achieved strong detection
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,774:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: performance. The key insight is that fake and real news stories generate structurally different propagation patterns.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,779:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: While this approach is promising, it requires the full propagation graph to be available, which limits its applicability
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,780:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: to early-stage detection. The NCPS, in contrast, computes credibility incrementally as each new vote arrives.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,780:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3. Multi-Modal Fake News Detection
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,783:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Wang et al. (2018) proposed the EANN model (Event Adversarial Neural Networks), which uses adversarial
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,784:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: training to learn event-invariant features for fake news detection 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,784:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,785:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 7
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,785:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,795:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . This approach attempts to address the
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,801:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: generalization problem — ensuring that models trained on one set of fake news stories can detect novel fabrications. Jin
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,802:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: et al. (2017) specifically addressed multi-modal fake news by jointly analyzing text and images using
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,803:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: attention-based RNNs 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,803:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,804:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 8
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,804:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,810:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . While multi-modal approaches represent the state-of-the-art in content analysis, they
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,811:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: fundamentally struggle with novel events that have no historical analogs, which is precisely the situation that
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,812:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: characterizes breaking local news.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,812:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 4. Linguistic Feature Analysis
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,817:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Perez-Rosas et al. (2018) took a more traditional NLP approach, identifying linguistic cues that distinguish fake
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,817:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: from real news, including the use of emotional language, personal pronouns, and hedging words 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,818:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,818:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 9
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,818:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,838:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . While their
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,856:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: analysis revealed interesting patterns (fake news tends to use more emotional and less analytic language), the feature
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,864:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: differences are statistical tendencies rather then definitive signals. A skilled fabricator could easily adjust their
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,867:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: writing style to avoid detection. The NCPS deliberately avoids content analysis for this reason, instead relying on
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,867:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: network-level signals that are much harder to manipulate.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,868:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 12 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,869:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2.2 Source and User Credibility Assessment
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,871:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Rather than analyzing content directly, source-based approaches focus on evaluating the credibility of the person or
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,871:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: entity sharing the information.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,872:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 5. Source Reliability in Social Networks (Shu et al., 2019)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,873:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Shu et al. conducted a comprehensive survey of fake news detection approaches, with particular emphasis on source
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,873:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: credibility features 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,874:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,874:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,874:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,910:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . They identified key source-level indicators including account age, posting frequency,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,936:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: follower-to-following ratio, and historical accuracy. Their framework, FakeNewsNet, provided benchmark datasets
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,951:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: that have been widely used in subsequent research. However, source features alone are insufficient because (a)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,958:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: newly created accounts may be legitimate, and (b) previously reliable sources can share misinformation
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,960:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: accidentally. The NCPS addresses this by not treating user reliability as a static label but as a continuously updated
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,960:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Bayesian estimate with confidence correction.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,961:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 6. Credibility Propagation in Information Networks (Gupta et al., 2012)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,963:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Gupta, Zhao, and Han proposed a credibility analysis framework that models the relationships between events,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,964:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: sources, and tweets as a heterogeneous information network 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,964:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,965:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 10
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,965:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,968:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . Credibility scores are propagated through the
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,969:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: network using an iterative algorithm similar to PageRank. This approach is conceptually similar to the NCPS
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,969:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,975:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s graph
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,979:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: trust propagation, but Gupta et al. do not incorporate anomaly detection or spatial signals, making their system
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,980:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: vulnerable to coordinated manipulation attacks where a group of accounts mutualy reinforce each other
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,981:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,981:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s credibility.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,982:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 7. User Profiling for Bot Detection (Varol et al., 2017)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,986:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Varol et al. developed Botometer (formerly BotOrNot), a machine learning-based tool that evaluates over 1,000
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,986:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: features of a Twitter account to estimate the likelihood that it is a bot 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,987:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,987:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 11
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:55,987:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,012:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . Features include temporal patterns,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,031:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: network structure, content analysis, and behavioral cues. While Botometer is highly effective for individual bot
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,041:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: detection, it requires access to platform-specific APIs and extensive historical data for each account. The NCPS
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,046:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: takes a different approach to bot detection through behavioral anomaly signals (burst patterns, coordination
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,046:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: detection, location inconsistencies) that can identify suspicious behavior even for accounts with limited history.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,047:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 13 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,048:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 8. Trust and Reputation Systems
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,049:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Josang, Ismail, and Boyd (2007) provided a foundational survey of trust and reputation systems for online services 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,049:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,049:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 12
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,050:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,050:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . They categorized approaches into centralized reputation (like eBay
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,051:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,081:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s feedback system), distributed reputation
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,106:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: (where trust is computed locally by each participant), and Bayesian reputation (where trust is modeled as a
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,120:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: probability distribution). The NCPS draws heavily from the Bayesian reputation paradigm, using Beta distributions
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,126:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: (parameterized by α and β counts) to model user reliability. However, unlike traditional reputation systems that rely
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,127:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: solely on direct evidence, the NCPS augments direct reliability estimates with graph-based trust propagation and
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,128:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: multi-signal anomaly detection.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,128:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2.3 Propagation-Based and Graph-Based Detection
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,131:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: These approaches analyze how information spreads through networks, recognizing that the propagation patterns of
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,131:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: true and false information tend to differ systematically.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,132:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 9. Rumor Detection with Graph Neural Networks (Bian et al., 2020)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,135:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Bian et al. proposed Bi-GCN (Bi-directional Graph Convolutional Network), which models both the top-down
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,136:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: propagation structure and the bottom-up aggregation structure of rumor threads 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,136:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,137:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 4
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,137:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,161:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . By applying graph convolutions
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,181:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: in both directions, the model captures how a rumor spreads from the source to followers (top-down) and how
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,193:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: community responses aggregate to form a collective assessment (bottom-up). Bi-GCN achieved state-of-the-art
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,198:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: results on Twitter15 and Twitter16 datasets. The key limitation, similar to other GNN approaches, is the requirement
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,198:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: for a substantially developed propagation tree before classification can be performed, which introduces detection
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,199:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: latency.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,199:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 10. Cascade-Based Early Detection (Ma et al., 2018)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,202:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Ma et al. explored the use of recurrent neural networks (specifically Tree-LSTMs) to model the temporal evolution
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,202:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: of information cascades for early rumor detection 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,202:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,203:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 13
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,203:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,225:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . Their approach can operate with partial cascade information,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,240:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: making it more suitable for early detection than full-graph methods. However, it still requires a minimum cascade
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,247:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: depth of 3-5 levels to achieve reasonable accuracy, and its performance degrades significently for cascades with
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,249:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: fewer than 10 nodes. In the local news context where many reports may recieve only a handful of interactions, this
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,249:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: limitation is particularly problematic.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,250:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 11. Network-Based Truth Discovery (Li et al., 2016)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,251:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Li et al. addressed the truth discovery problem — estimating the veracity of claims when multiple sources provide
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,251:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: conflicting information 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,252:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,252:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 14
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,252:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,255:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . Their approach jointly estimates source reliability and claim truthfulness through an
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,256:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: iterative optimization process. This is conceptually closely related to the NCPS
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,256:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,264:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s approach, where user reliability
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,269:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: and post credibility are simultaneously estimated. However, Li et al. do not incorporate graph structure, spatial
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,270:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: information, or anomaly detection, and their framework is designed for static datasets rather then streaming,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,271:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: real-time scenarios.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,272:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 15 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,273:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 12. Social Network Analysis for Influence Detection (Kempe et al., 2003)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,273:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: While not directly focused on misinformation, Kempe, Kleinberg, and Tardos
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,274:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,274:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  foundational work on influence
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,275:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: maximization in social networks 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,275:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,275:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 15
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,276:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,303:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  established the theoretical framework for understanding how information
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,323:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: propagates through graph structures. Their greedy algorithm for influence maximization demonstrated that network
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,333:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: topology plays a crucial role in determining which nodes have the greatest impact on information spread. The NCPS
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,337:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: leverages similar network-topological insights, but inverts the objective: rather than maximizing influence, we aim
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,338:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: to minimize the spread of unreliable content by dampening the influence of untrustworthy nodes.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,339:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2.4 Truth Discovery and Crowdsourced Verification
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,340:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Truth discovery approaches treat users as sources with varying reliability and attempt to estimate both source quality
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,341:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: and claim veracity simultaneously.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,341:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 13. Truth Discovery with Conflicting Information Providers (Yin et al., 2008)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,342:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Yin, Han, and Yu proposed one of the earliest truth discovery frameworks 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,343:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,343:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 16
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,343:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,396:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: , addressing the fundamental
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,445:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: challenge of determining factual truth when multiple information providers give conflicting statements. Their
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,479:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: approach iteratively refines source reliability estimates and fact confidence scores until convergence. The key
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,501:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: insight is that reliable sources tend to provide accurate information, and accurate information tends to be provided
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,514:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: by reliable sources. This circular dependency is resolved through an iterative algorithm analogous to
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,520:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: expectation-maximization. The NCPS builds upon this foundational concept but significantly extends it by
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,521:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: incorporating temporal decay, anomaly detection, and graph-based trust signals that are not present in the original
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,522:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: truth discovery framework.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,522:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 14. Crowdsourced Fact-Checking (Allen et al., 2021)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,524:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Allen et al. (2021) studied the effectiveness of crowdsourced fact-checking, where ordinary users rate the accuracy
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,524:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: of news articles 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,525:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,525:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 17
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,526:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,528:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . Surprisingly, they found that aggregated crowd assessments showed high agreement with
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,528:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: professional fact-checkers, suggesting that the 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,529:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,529:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: wisdom of crowds
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,529:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: "
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,535:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  can be leveraged for credibility assessment.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,538:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: However, their study also identified vulnerability to manipulation — when a sufficiently large group of users coordinates
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,539:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: to rate false content as true, the crowd
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,539:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,540:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s assessment can be corrupted. This vulnerability motivated the NCPS
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,540:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,543:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,546:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: multi-layered defense mechanism, particularly the coordination detection module that identifies and penalizes
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,546:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: groups of users who exhibit suspiciously similar voting patterns.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,547:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 15. Community Notes (Twitter/X)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,547:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Twitter
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,547:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,549:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s Community Notes program (formerly Birdwatch) represents perhaps the most prominent real-world
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,549:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: deployment of crowdsourced fact-checking 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,549:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,550:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 18
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,550:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,603:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . The system allows users to write notes providing context or
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,645:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: corrections to potentially misleading tweets. Notes are shown to a broad audience only if users from diverse political
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,672:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: perspectives agree on their helpfulness. While Community Notes has shown promise for high-visibility viral
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,686:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: content, it is fundamentally designed for a different scale — it targets tweets that have already gone viral, whereas
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,693:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: NCPS operates on local reports that may have only a handful of interactions. Additionally, Community Notes relies
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,695:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: on a bridging-based consensus algorithm that requires substantial participation volumes to function effectively,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,695:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: which is impractical for hyper-local content.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,696:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 17 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,697:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2.5 Location-Aware Information Systems
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,699:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The spatial dimension of information credibility has received comparatively less attention in the literature, despite
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,699:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: its relevance to local news verification.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,700:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 16. Location-Based Social Network Analysis (Cho et al., 2011)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,702:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Cho, Myers, and Leskovec studied mobility patterns in location-based social networks, finding that social network
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,703:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ties significantly influence individual mobility patterns 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,703:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,703:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 19
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,704:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,717:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . Their work demonstrated that geographic information
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,724:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: can provide valuable signals for understanding user behavior and detecting anomalies. Users who claim to be in
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,727:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: vastly different locations within short time spans, or who exhibit teleporting behavior, are likely either spoofing their
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,727:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: location or using compromised accounts. The NCPS
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,728:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,730:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s spatial engine incorporates similar insights, using location
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,730:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: consistency metrics and device fingerprinting to assess user trustworthiness.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,731:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 17. Geospatial Information Credibility (Goodchild and Glennon, 2010)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,737:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Goodchild and Glennon explored the concept of spatial data quality in the context of volunteered geographic
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,738:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: information (VGI), arguing that the credibility of user-contributed spatial data can be partially assessed through
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,739:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: geographic consistency checks 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,739:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,740:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 20
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,740:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,756:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . Reports that are geographically inconsistent (e.g., a user claiming to witness an
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,765:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: event while located far from the reported event location) should receive lower credibility. The NCPS implements
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,768:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: this principle through its proximity weighting function, which applies Gaussian distance decay to reduce the
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,769:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: influence of votes from users located far from the reported event.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,769:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2.6 Trust Propagation in Networks
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,772:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Trust propagation approaches leverage the transitive nature of trust — if A trusts B and B trusts C, then A has some
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,772:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: basis for trusting C, albeit with decreased confidence.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,773:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 18. EigenTrust (Kamvar et al., 2003)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,774:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Kamvar, Schlosser, and Garcia-Molina proposed EigenTrust, a reputation management algorithm for peer-to-peer
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,774:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: networks 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,775:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,775:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 21
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,775:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,781:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . EigenTrust computes global trust values by iteratively aggregating local trust relationships, similar to
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,782:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: how PageRank aggregates link authority. The algorithm converges to a unique steady-state vector that represents
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,782:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: each node
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,783:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,783:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s global reputation. The NCPS
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,784:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,786:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s graph trust propagation is inspired by EigenTrust but incorporates a
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,787:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: critical safety constraint: trust can never be inflated beyond a user
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,787:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,788:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s individual reliability (T
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,788:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,789:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i ≤ R
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,789:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: *
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,789:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,791:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i). This constraint,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,792:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: which is absent in EigenTrust, prevents colluding groups from artificially boosting each other
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,793:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,793:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s trust scores.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,794:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 19. TrustRank (Gyöngyi et al., 2004)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,799:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Gyöngyi, Garcia-Molina, and Pedersen developed TrustRank for combating web spam, demonstrating how trust can
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,800:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: be propagated from a small set of manually verified seed nodes to the rest of a web graph 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,800:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,800:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 22
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,801:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,817:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . The key insight is
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,830:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: that trustworthy pages tend to link to other trustworthy pages, allowing trust to be estimated for pages that have not
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,835:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: been manually reviewed. While the NCPS does not assume the existence of pre-verified seed users, it leverages a
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,837:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: similar propagation mechanism where well-behaved users (identified through Bayesian reliability estimation) serve
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,837:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: as implicit trust anchors.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,838:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 20 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,838:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2.7 Anomaly Detection in User Behavior
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,839:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Detecting anomalous behavior is crucial for identifying manipulation attempts in online platforms.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,840:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 20. Bot Detection Through Temporal Analysis (Cresci et al., 2017)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,843:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Cresci et al. demonstrated that simple feature-based bot detection can be evaded by sophisticated social bots, and
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,844:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: proposed DNA-inspired techniques that model user behavior as sequences of actions 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,844:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,845:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 23
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,845:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,848:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . By analyzing the
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,849:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: temporal patterns of these action sequences, they could identify bots even when individual features appeared
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,849:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: human-like. The NCPS
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,850:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,855:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s temporal anomaly detection (burst detection, entropy analysis) is motivated by similar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,859:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: observations — coordinated bots tend to exhibit temporally regular patterns that differ from the naturally irregular
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,860:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: patterns of human behavior.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,860:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 21. Coordinated Inauthentic Behavior Detection (Nizzoli et al., 2021)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,862:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Nizzoli et al. studied coordinated inauthentic behavior on social media, where groups of accounts work together to
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,862:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: manipulate public discourse 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,863:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,863:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 24
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,863:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,887:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . They identified key signatures of coordination, including temporal
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,905:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: synchronization (accounts posting or engaging at the same times), content alignment (accounts sharing the same or
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,914:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: similar content), and network clustering (accounts forming densely connected subgroups). The NCPS implements
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,917:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: coordination detection by building a user graph based on voting agreement, temporal proximity, and interaction
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,918:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: frequency, then applying link dampening to edges within identified coordinated clusters.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,919:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 21 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:56,919:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2.8 Summary of Literature Survey
