   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,051:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 24
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,051:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,054:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  | Temporal, content, and network
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,056:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: coordination signals | Coordinated inauthentic behavior | Identified coordinated campaigns | Detection only; no
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,056:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: integrated mitigation |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,057:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: From the literature review, we identify several key gaps that the NCPS addresses:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,057:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  1 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,058:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: No unified system
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,060:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  combines Bayesian credibility estimation, graph trust propagation, anomaly
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,061:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: detection, spatial awareness, and ML augmentation in a single framework.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,062:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,062:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Real-time operation
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,063:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  is rarely addressed — most approaches are designed for post-hoc analysis rather
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,064:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: then streaming credibility estimation.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,064:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,065:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Local news context
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,065:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  is largely ignored — existing systems target viral content on major platforms.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,066:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  4 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,066:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Coordinated attack resistance
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,068:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  through integrated detection and mitigation (rather than just
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,069:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: detection) is not present in any existing system.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,069:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  5 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,070:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Geographic propagation control
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,071:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  — adjusting content reach based on credibility — is a novel concept not
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,071:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: found in the literature.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,080:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The NCPS addresses all five gaps by combining established techniques (Bayesian estimation, trust propagation,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,083:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: anomaly detection) with novel contributions (conservative design philosophy, 5-condition propagation gate, spatial
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,084:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: trust integration) in a unified, real-time system for local news verification.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,085:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 24 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,086:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="page-break-after: always;"></div>
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,087:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: CHAPTER 3
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,087:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: PROPOSED METHODOLOGY
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,096:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: This chapter presents the complete technical design of the Network-aware Credibility and Propagation System
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,099:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: (NCPS). We describe the system architecture, mathematical formulation, algorithms, and implementation details
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,100:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: that together form a comprehensive credibility-driven platform for local news verification.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,100:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3.1 Problem Statement
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,101:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Given the gaps identified in the literature review, we formalize the problem that NCPS aims to solve.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,101:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Input
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,102:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : A stream of events comprising:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,102:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,103:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: User registrations with geographic coordinates
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,103:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,104:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: User-submitted news reports (posts) with content and location
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,104:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,104:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Community votes (upvote +1 or downvote -1) on existing posts
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,105:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Output
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,105:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : For each post, a credibility score C ∈ 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,105:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,106:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 0, 1
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,106:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,107:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  and a propagation decision (expand/hold). For each user, a
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,108:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: composite weight w ∈ 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,108:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,108:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 0, 1
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,108:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,109:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  reflecting their estimated trustworthiness.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,109:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Constraints
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,110:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: :
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,110:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  1 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,111:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The system must be conservative — trust can decrease through manipulation but can never be
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,112:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: artificially inflated above individual merit
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,112:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,113:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Credibility computation must be incremental — each new vote should immediately update the post
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,113:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,114:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,114:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: credibility without requiring full recomputation
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,114:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,116:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The system must be resistant to coordinated manipulation — groups of colluding accounts should not be
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,116:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: able to game credibility scores
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,117:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  4 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,117:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Geographic propagation must be controlled — unverified content should not spread beyond its locality
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,118:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 25 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,119:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3.2 System Architecture Overview
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,137:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The NCPS follows a layered architecture pattern with clear separation of concerns between the presentation layer,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,145:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: application logic, computation engines, and data persistence. The architecture is designed to be modular — each
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,148:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: computation engine operates independently and can be added or removed without affecting the others, which
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,148:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: enabled the phased development approach described in Section 3.7.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,149:      pdf_renderer.py:  235: /Users/chandraprakash/.gemini/antigravity/brain/608c58f2-8d2c-4b04-972b-ca1c9279e9d7/fig_3_1_ncps_architecture_1780257517758.png, 1024, 1024
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,155:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Fig 3.1: NCPS System Architecture showing four distinct layers — Client Layer (React App, Web Browser), API
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,156:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Gateway (FastAPI with REST endpoints), Computation Layer (six engines), and Data Layer (PostgreSQL, Redis,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,156:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Kafka)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,156:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: As illustrated in Fig 3.1, the system comprises four distinct layers:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,157:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Client Layer
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,166:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : The user-facing interface built with React (for the rich interactive dashboard) and vanilla JavaScript
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,169:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: with HTML/CSS (for the primary web application). The client communicates with the backend exclusively through
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,169:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: REST API calls, ensuring a clean separation between frontend and backend concerns.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,170:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: API Gateway
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,175:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : A FastAPI-based REST API server that handles authentication (JWT-based), request validation, and
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,177:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: routing. The gateway exposes endpoints for user management, post operations, voting, feed retrieval, map data,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,177:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: profile information, and analytics.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,178:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Computation Layer
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,178:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Six specialized engines that collectively implement the credibility assessment pipeline:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,179:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,179:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: User Engine
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,179:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,180:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: user_engine.py
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,180:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ): Computes reliability, confidence, experience, and final user
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,181:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: weights
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,181:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,181:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Post Engine
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,182:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,182:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: post_engine.py
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,182:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ): Computes Bayesian credibility, variance, and evidence mass
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,183:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,183:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Graph Engine
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,183:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,184:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: graph_engine.py
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,184:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ): Builds the user interaction graph, detects coordination, and
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,185:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: propagates trust
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,185:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,185:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Spatial Engine
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,186:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,186:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: spatial.py
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,187:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ): Computes location confidence, proximity weights, and manages
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,187:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: propagation radius
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,187:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,188:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ML Engine
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,188:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,188:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ml_engine.py
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,189:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ): Provides machine learning predictions and memory-based
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,189:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: similarity scores
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,190:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,190:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Decision Engine
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,190:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,191:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: decision.py
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,191:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ): Evaluates the 5-condition gate for propagation decisions and
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,192:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: generates alerts
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,192:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Data Layer
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,199:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : PostgreSQL serves as the primary relational database, with tables for user accounts, user state, posts,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,200:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: interactions, locations, and the user graph. Redis provides caching for frequently accessed data, and Kafka handles
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,201:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: event streaming for asynchronous processing.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,202:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 27 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,203:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3.3 Detailed Architecture
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,203:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3.3.1 Event-Driven Data Model
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,204:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The NCPS processes three fundamental event types, each triggering a cascade of state updates across the
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,205:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: computation engines:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,205:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Registration Event
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,229:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : When a new user registers, the system creates an authentication account and initializes a user
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,243:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: profile with default Bayesian priors (α₀ = 1, β₀ = 1, representing maximum uncertainty), zero experience, zero anomaly
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,248:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: score, and the provided geographic coordinates. The initial reliability R = α/(α+β) = 0.5 and confidence is near zero,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,249:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: reflecting the principle that new users should have minimal influence until they establish a track record.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,250:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Post Event
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,251:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : When a user creates a post, the system stores the content, location (latitude, longitude), urgency
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,252:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: classification, and initializes the post
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,252:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,253:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s credibility with agnostic priors (α₀ = 1, β₀ = 1, giving C
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,253:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,255:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Bayes = 0.5). The post
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,255:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: is assigned an initial propagation radius based on the user
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,256:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,256:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s weight and the urgency level.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,257:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Vote Event
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,258:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : This is the most complex event type and triggers the majority of computation. When user i votes on
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,258:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: post j:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,258:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  1 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,259:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The user
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,259:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,260:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s current weight w
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,260:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,261:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i is fetched (or computed if stale)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,261:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,262:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The vote (v ∈ {-1, +1}) is weighted by w
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,262:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,263:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i and applied to the post
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,263:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,263:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s evidence accumulators
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,264:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,264:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The post
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,265:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,265:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s Bayesian credibility is recomputed
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,266:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  4 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,266:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: If anomaly detection is enabled, the user
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,267:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,267:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s behavioral signals are updated
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,268:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  5 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,268:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: If graph trust is enabled, the user graph edges are updated based on vote agreement patterns
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,269:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  6 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,269:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The propagation decision is re-evaluated
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,275:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: This event-driven model ensures that credibility scores are always up-to-date and that the system responds
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,276:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: immediately to new information. There is no batch processing step — every vote triggers an immediate incremental
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,277:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: update.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,278:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 28 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,278:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3.3.2 User State Computation Pipeline
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,282:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The User Engine maintains a comprehensive state profile for each user, combining multiple signals into a single
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,283:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: composite weight. The pipeline, illustrated in Fig 3.2, proceeds through several stages.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,284:      pdf_renderer.py:  235: /Users/chandraprakash/.gemini/antigravity/brain/608c58f2-8d2c-4b04-972b-ca1c9279e9d7/fig_3_3_user_weight_pipeline_1780257532114.png, 1024, 1024
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,290:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Fig 3.2: User Weight Computation Pipeline showing the flow from raw user actions through Bayesian reliability,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,291:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: confidence correction, experience weighting, anomaly detection, graph trust, to the final composite weight
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,291:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Stage 1: Raw Reliability Estimation
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,292:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Each user is modeled as a Bernoulli information source with unknown reliability parameter p
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,292:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,293:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i. We maintain
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,293:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: conjugate Beta prior counts α
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,293:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,294:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i (positive evidence) and β
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,294:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,295:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i (negative evidence). The raw reliability is simply the
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,296:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: mean of the Beta distribution:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,296:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: $$R
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,296:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,296:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i = 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,297:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,297:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: frac{
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,297:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,297:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: alpha
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,298:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,298:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i}{
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,298:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,298:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: alpha
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,298:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,299:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i + 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,299:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,299:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: beta
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,299:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,300:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i}$$
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,314:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: When a user votes correctly (their vote aligns with the eventual credibility outcome), α is incremented. When they
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,319:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: vote incorrectly, β is incremented. This Bayesian approach naturally handles uncertainty — a user with α=10, β=2 (R=0.83)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,319:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: is much more trusted than a user with α=1, β=0 (R=1.0) because the former has substantially more evidence.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,320:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Stage 2: Confidence Correction
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,320:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Raw reliability alone is insufficient because it doesn
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,321:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,324:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t account for the amount of evidence. A user with α=1, β=0 has a
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,324:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: reliability of 1.0 but essentially zero evidence. To address this, we compute a confidence factor:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,325:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: $$Conf
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,325:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,325:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i = 1 - 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,326:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,326:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: exp(-k 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,326:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,327:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: cdot (
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,327:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,327:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: alpha
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,327:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,328:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i + 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,328:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,328:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: beta
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,328:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,329:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i))$$
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,332:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: where k is the evidence growth rate (default k=0.1). This produces a value close to 0 for users with little evidence
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,332:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: and approaches 1 as evidence accumulates. The effective reliability combines both:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,333:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: $$R^
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,333:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: *
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,333:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,334:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i = R
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,334:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,334:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,334:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,335:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: times Conf
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,335:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,335:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i$$
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,346:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: This elegant formulation ensures that new users with high nominal reliability but low evidence are appropriately
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,349:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: discounted. It was one of the first design decisions we made, and in retrospect it turned out to be crucial for
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,350:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: preventing attacks that create many fresh accounts to manipulate credibility scores.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,351:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 30 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,351:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Stage 3: Experience Weighting
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,355:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Beyond reliability, we also value experience — users who have contributed more interactions have demonstrated
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,355:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: sustained engagement with the platform. The experience score uses logarithmic scaling:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,358:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: $$Exp
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,358:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,359:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i = 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,359:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,359:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: frac{
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,360:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,360:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: log(1 + E
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,360:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,361:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i)}{
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,361:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,361:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: log(1 + E
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,362:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,362:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: {max})}$$
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,362:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: where E
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,363:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,363:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i is user i
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,363:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,364:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s total interaction count and E
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,364:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,370:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: max is a configurable maximum (default 100). The logarithmic
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,371:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: function ensures diminishing returns — the difference between 0 and 10 interactions is much more significant than the
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,372:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: difference between 90 and 100.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,372:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Stage 4: Anomaly Detection
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,373:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The anomaly detection subsystem monitors five independent behavioral signals:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,373:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  1 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,374:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Burst Score
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,374:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (S
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,374:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,375:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: burst): Detects unusually rapid voting activity. If a user casts more than 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,375:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: max_actions_per_window
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,376:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  votes within 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,377:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: burst_window_seconds
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,377:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: , the burst score
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,378:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: increases proportionally.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,378:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,379:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Entropy Score
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,379:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (S
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,379:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,380:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: entropy): Measures the diversity of a user
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,380:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,385:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s voting pattern. Normal users should
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,388:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: exhibit a mix of upvotes and downvotes across different posts. A perfectly uniform voting pattern
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,389:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: (e.g., always upvoting) results in low entropy, which is suspicious.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,389:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,389:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Consensus Deviation
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,390:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (S
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,390:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,397:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: consensus): Measures how often a user disagrees with the emerging
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,399:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: consensus on posts. Users who consistently vote against the majority on posts that ultimately
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,400:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: converge to high or low credibility are flagged as potentially adversarial.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,401:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  4 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,401:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Coordination Score
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,401:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (S
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,402:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,402:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: coord): Measures the degree to which a user
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,403:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,406:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s voting pattern correlates with
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,406:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: other users in terms of both timing and direction. High coordination scores indicate potential botnet
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,407:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: activity.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,407:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  5 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,408:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Location Anomaly
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,408:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  (S
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,409:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,414:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: location): Detects geographic inconsistencies such as teleporting (claiming
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,415:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: to be in vastly different locations within a short time) or using an unusually high number of devices
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,415:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: or IP addresses.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,416:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The composite anomaly score is the weighted mean:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,416:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: $$Anom
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,417:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,417:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i = 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,418:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,418:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: frac{1}{5} 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,419:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,419:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: sum
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,420:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,420:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: {s=1}^{5} S
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,421:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,421:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: {s,i}$$
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,422:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: All anomaly sub-scores are clamped to 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,422:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,422:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 0, 1
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,423:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,423:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: , so the composite anomaly score is also in 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,424:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,424:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 0, 1
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,425:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,426:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: . A score above 0.3 is
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,427:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: considered anomalous in the default configuration.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,427:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Stage 5: Final Weight Computation
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,428:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The final user weight combines trust (from graph propagation), anomaly suppression, and experience:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,428:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: $$w
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,428:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,429:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i = T
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,429:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,429:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,429:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,430:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: times (1 - Anom
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,430:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,430:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i) 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,430:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,431:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: times Exp
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,431:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,431:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i$$
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,431:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: where T
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,432:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,432:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i is the graph-based trust score (Section 3.3.4). If graph trust is not enabled, T
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,432:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,433:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i defaults to R
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,433:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: *
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,433:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,447:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i (the
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,460:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: effective reliability). This multiplicative formulation is deliberate — any single dimension of untrustworthiness (low
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,464:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: trust, high anomaly, or zero experience) drives the weight towards zero. This conservative approach ensures that a
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,465:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: compromised account cannot compensate for detected anomalies by having high graph trust, or vice versa.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,466:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 31 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,466:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3.3.3 Post Credibility Computation Pipeline
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,471:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The Post Engine computes the credibility of each post through weighted aggregation of community votes,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,472:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: supplemented by machine learning predictions and historical memory. The pipeline is illustrated in Fig 3.3.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,473:      pdf_renderer.py:  235: /Users/chandraprakash/.gemini/antigravity/brain/608c58f2-8d2c-4b04-972b-ca1c9279e9d7/fig_3_4_post_credibility_pipeline_1780257576955.png, 1024, 1024
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,479:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Fig 3.3: Post Credibility Computation Pipeline showing the flow from user votes through positive/negative evidence
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,479:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: aggregation, Bayesian estimation, ML and memory augmentation, to the final credibility score
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,480:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Weighted Evidence Aggregation
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,480:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: When user i casts vote v
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,481:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,481:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i ∈ {-1, +1} on post j, the vote is weighted by the user
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,481:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,481:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s current weight w
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,482:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,483:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i and a temporal
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,483:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: decay factor that reduces the influence of older votes:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,483:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: $$decay(t) = 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,484:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,484:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: exp(-
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,484:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,485:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: lambda
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,485:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,485:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: {decay} 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,486:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,486:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: cdot 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,486:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,486:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Delta t)$$
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,487:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: where Δt is the time elapsed since the vote and λ
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,487:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,488:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: decay controls the decay rate. Votes are then accumulated into
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,489:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: positive and negative evidence streams:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,489:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: $$S^+ = 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,489:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
