   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,594:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ml = 0.15 and γ
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,594:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,597:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: mem = 0.10 by default, ensuring that the Bayesian estimate (which is principled and
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,598:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: interpretable) remains the dominant signal while ML and memory provide supplementary corrections.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,599:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3.3.4 Graph Trust and Coordination Detection
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,604:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The Graph Engine is responsible for two interrelated tasks: (1) detecting coordinated manipulation and (2)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,605:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: propagating trust through the user interaction graph. This component, introduced in Phase 3, significantly improved
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,606:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: the system
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,606:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,607:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s resilience against organized attacks.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,608:      pdf_renderer.py:  235: /Users/chandraprakash/.gemini/antigravity/brain/608c58f2-8d2c-4b04-972b-ca1c9279e9d7/fig_3_5_graph_trust_1780257592924.png, 1024, 1024
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,615:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Fig 3.4: Graph Trust and Coordination Detection showing the user interaction network with honest (green) and bot
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,616:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: (red) users, the coordination detection pipeline, and the trust propagation formula with convergence constraint
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,616:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Building the User Graph
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,618:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The user interaction graph G = (V, E) is constructed from voting co-occurrence patterns. An edge between users i
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,619:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: and j is weighted by three factors:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,619:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  1 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,619:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Agreement
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,620:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : How often users i and j vote the same way on the same posts
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,620:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,620:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Temporal Proximity
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,621:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : How close in time their votes occur (coordinated bots tend to vote within
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,622:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: seconds of each other)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,622:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,622:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Frequency
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,623:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : How many posts they have both voted on
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,623:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The edge weight captures the overall similarity between two users
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,624:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,626:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  voting behaviors. High edge weights between
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,627:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: users who both exhibit suspicious behavior (high anomaly scores) are strong indicators of coordination.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,628:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 33 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,628:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Coordination Detection
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,631:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Once the graph is constructed, coordination detection proceeds by identifying clusters of highly connected nodes
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,632:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: with similar behavioral profiles. The algorithm works as follows:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,632:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  1 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,634:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: For each pair of connected users, compute a coordination score based on the combination of high
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,634:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: agreement, temporal synchronization, and high interaction frequency
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,635:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,635:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: If the coordination score exceeds a threshold (coord
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,635:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,636:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: threshold = 0.7), the users are flagged as
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,636:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: potentially coordinated
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,637:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,637:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Edges within coordinated clusters are dampened by a factor (link
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,637:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,638:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: dampen
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,638:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,639:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: factor = 0.1),
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,639:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: dramatically reducing the trust flow between colluding users
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,640:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  4 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,640:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The effective reliability (R
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,640:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: *
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,641:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ) of users within coordinated groups is penalized
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,651:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: This approach is effective because genuine users rarely exhibit the precise behavioral synchronization that
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,654:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: characterizes bot networks. Even when individual bot accounts are sophisticated enough to pass simple detection
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,655:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: methods, the statistical signature of their coordination is much harder to conceal.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,655:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Trust Propagation
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,657:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: After coordination detection and edge dampening, trust is propagated through the graph using an iterative process
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,657:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: inspired by EigenTrust 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,657:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,658:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 21
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,658:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,658:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: :
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,659:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: $$T^{(k+1)} = 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,659:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,659:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: lambda 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,660:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,660:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: cdot A
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,660:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,661:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: {norm} 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,661:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,662:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: cdot T^{(k)} + (1 - 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,662:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,662:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: lambda) 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,663:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,663:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: cdot R^
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,663:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: *
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,664:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: $$
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,664:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: where A
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,664:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,665:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: norm is the row-normalized adjacency matrix, λ is the damping factor (default 0.5), and R
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,665:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: *
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,667:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  is the vector of
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,668:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: effective reliabilities. This is iterated until convergence (typically 10-15 iterations with tolerance 1e-6).
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,668:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The critical safety constraint is enforced after convergence:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,669:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: $$T
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,669:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,669:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i = 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,670:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,670:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: min(T
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,670:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,671:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i, R^
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,671:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: *
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,671:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,672:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i)$$
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,672:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: This constraint ensures that trust propagation can only reduce a user
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,673:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,676:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s trust (by spreading distrust from compromised
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,677:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: neighbors), never inflate it. Without this constraint, a group of colluding bots could boost each other
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,677:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,679:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s trust scores
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,679:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: through the propagation mechanism. With it, the system maintains its conservative guarantee.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,680:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 34 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,681:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3.3.5 Spatial Trust and Location Confidence
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,684:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The Spatial Engine, introduced in Phase 4, adds geographic awareness to the credibility assessment. It operates on
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,684:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: two levels: user-level location confidence and post-level propagation control.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,686:      pdf_renderer.py:  235: /Users/chandraprakash/.gemini/antigravity/brain/608c58f2-8d2c-4b04-972b-ca1c9279e9d7/fig_3_6_spatial_propagation_1780257849963.png, 1024, 1024
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,692:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Fig 3.5: Spatial Trust and Propagation Decision Workflow showing concentric propagation circles, the 5-condition
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,693:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: AND gate for radius expansion, and the Gaussian distance decay proximity formula
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,693:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Location Confidence
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,695:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The location confidence of a user is computed from three independent signals, all of which are designed to detect
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,695:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: common spoofing behaviors:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,695:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  1 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,696:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Location Consistency
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,703:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Users who frequently teleport (appearing in geographically distant locations
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,706:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: within short time periods) receive lower location confidence. The consistency score is computed by
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,706:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: analyzing the history of location updates and flagging physically impossible movements.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,707:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,707:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Device Count
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,707:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Each user
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,708:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,711:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s distinct device fingerprints are tracked. Normal users typically access the
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,711:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: platform from 1-3 devices. Users showing 5+ distinct devices are penalized (the default max
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,712:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,712:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: devices threshold is 5).
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,713:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,713:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: IP Diversity
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,716:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Similar to device count, an unusually high number of distinct IP addresses (especially
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,716:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: from geographically diverse locations) indicates potential bot activity. The default max
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,717:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,717:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ips
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,717:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: threshold is 10.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,718:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The composite location confidence is:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,718:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: $$L
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,718:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,718:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i = 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,719:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,719:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: frac{loc
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,719:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,719:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: consistency
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,720:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,720:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i + device
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,720:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,720:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: score
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,721:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,721:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i + ip
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,721:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,721:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: score
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,722:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,722:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i}{3}$$
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,722:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: where each component is normalized to 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,723:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,723:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 0, 1
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,723:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,723:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: .
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,724:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 35 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,725:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Proximity Weighting
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,725:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: When a user votes on a post, their vote
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,726:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,727:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s influence is modulated by their geographic proximity to the reported event.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,728:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The proximity function uses Gaussian distance decay:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,728:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: $$P(d) = 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,728:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,729:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: exp
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,729:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,729:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: left(-
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,730:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,730:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: frac{d^2}{2
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,730:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,731:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: sigma^2}
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,731:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: \
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,731:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: right)$$
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,732:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: where d is the Haversine distance between the user
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,732:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,732:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s location and the post
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,732:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,748:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s location, and σ is the proximity standard
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,758:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: deviation (default 5.0 km). This means that users located near the reported event have significantly more influence
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,761:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: on its credibility score than distant users, which makes intuitive sense — a witness to a local event provides more
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,762:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: reliable information than someone speculating from across the country.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,762:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Propagation Radius Management
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,763:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The propagation radius determines how far a post
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,763:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,764:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s visibility extends geographically. It starts at a base value
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,764:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: (proportional to the creator
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,765:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,765:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s weight) and can expand only if the post meets five stringent conditions:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,766:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  1 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,766:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Credibility
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,766:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : C
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,767:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,767:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: final ≥ 0.6
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,767:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,768:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Evidence Mass
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,768:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : N ≥ 3.0 (at least 3 weighted votes)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,769:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,769:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Variance
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,769:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Var ≤ 0.25 (community largely agrees)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,770:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  4 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,770:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Age
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,771:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Post age ≥ 60 seconds (prevent premature expansion)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,771:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  5 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,771:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Location Trust
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,772:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Mean location confidence of voters ≥ 0.3
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,781:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: All five conditions must be satisfied simultaneously (AND gate). If any single condition fails, the radius remains
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,783:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: unchanged. When all conditions are met, the radius increases by a step increment (default 0.5 km), up to a maximum
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,783:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: radius determined by the credibility level.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,787:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: This 5-condition gate embodies the conservative philosophy of NCPS. Its actually quite strict — a post needs to be
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,788:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: well-supported, consistent, mature, and verified by geographically trustworthy users before it
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,788:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,799:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s allowed to reach a
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,806:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: wider audience. We considered relaxing some of these conditions during development but ultimately decided that
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,809:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: the conservative approach was preferable, because the cost of spreading misinformation far outweighs the cost of
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,809:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: slightly delaying the spread of true information.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,811:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 36 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,812:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3.3.6 ML and Memory Augmentation
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,813:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The ML Engine, introduced in Phase 5, provides two supplementary credibility signals that complement the
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,814:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: principled Bayesian estimation.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,814:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Machine Learning Prediction (C
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,815:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,815:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ML)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,816:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The ML component uses scikit-learn
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,816:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,818:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s LogisticRegression classifier, trained on resolved posts with known ground
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,819:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: truth labels. The feature vector for each post includes:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,819:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,820:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Variance-to-evidence ratio: Var/N
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,820:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,820:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Mean voter weight: mean(w
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,821:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,821:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i for voters of post j)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,821:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,822:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Standard deviation of voter weights
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,822:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,822:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Temporal spread of votes (time between first and last vote)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,822:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,823:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Anomaly concentration (fraction of voters with anomaly score > 0.3)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,833:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The choice of Logistic Regression over more complex models (gradient boosting, neural networks) was deliberate.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,837:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: In the simulation setting with relatively few training examples, simpler models tend to generalize better.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,837:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Additionally, Logistic Regression provides calibrated probability outputs, which is important because C
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,837:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,838:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ML is
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,838:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: combined with C
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,838:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,840:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Bayes in a weighted average — the combination is only meaningful if both components are on the
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,840:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: same probabilistic scale.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,840:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Memory-Based Similarity (C
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,841:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,841:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: memory)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,857:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The memory module maintains a TF-IDF vectorizer fitted on the content of all historically resolved posts. When a
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,864:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: new post arrives, its content is vectorized and compared against the memory bank using cosine similarity. If the
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,865:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: most similar historical post had a credibility score below 0.3 (indicating false information), the memory score biases
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,865:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: the new post
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,866:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,866:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s credibility downward proportionally to the similarity.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,872:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: This mechanism is particularly effective against recycled misinformation — false claims that resurface with slightly
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,873:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: different wording. While the text may be superficially different, the TF-IDF representation captures the underlying
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,873:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: topical similarity.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,874:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 37 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,875:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3.3.7 Propagation Decision Engine
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,878:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The Decision Engine is the final component in the processing pipeline, responsible for integrating all signals into
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,878:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: actionable propagation decisions and user alerts.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,879:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Propagation Decision
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,881:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The propagation decision for each post is governed by the 5-condition AND gate described in Section 3.3.5. When
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,882:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: all conditions are met, the post
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,883:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,884:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s propagation radius is expanded. The expansion rate is proportional to the credibility
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,884:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: level:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,885:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,885:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: C
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,885:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,886:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: final ∈ 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,886:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,887:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 0.6, 0.75): Slow expansion (0.3 km per step)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,887:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,887:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: C
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,888:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,888:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: final ∈ 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,888:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: [
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,889:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 0.75, 0.9): Medium expansion (0.5 km per step)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,889:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: l
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,890:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: C
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,890:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,891:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: final ≥ 0.9: Fast expansion (1.0 km per step)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,891:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Alert Generation
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,892:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The Decision Engine also monitors for conditions that warrant user alerts:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,892:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  1 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,893:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Low Credibility Alert
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,894:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : If a post
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,894:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,895:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s credibility drops below 0.3 with evidence mass > 5, an alert is
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,896:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: generated for the post creator
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,896:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  2 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,897:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Anomaly Alert
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,897:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : If a user
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,898:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,899:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s anomaly score exceeds 0.5, they receive a warning about suspicious
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,899:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: activity patterns
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,899:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  3 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,900:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Propagation Block Alert
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,902:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : If a post that previously qualified for expansion loses one or more
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,902:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: conditions, an alert notifies relevant users
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,905:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Alerts are rate-limited using a per-user alert limit system to prevent notification fatigue. Each user can receive a
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,906:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: maximum of 3 alerts per 24-hour period by default.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,907:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 38 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:57,907:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3.4 Mathematical Formulation
