   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,064:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: These 14 signals are the raw inputs from which all derived quantities (R, R
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,065:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: *
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,065:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: , Conf, Exp, Anom, T, w, C
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,066:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,066:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Bayes, C
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,066:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,067:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ML, C
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,067:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,067:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: memory, C
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,068:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,073:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: final, Var, N, propagation decision) are computed. The diversity of signals — spanning behavioral,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,074:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: temporal, geographic, and content dimensions — makes the system robust against manipulation strategies that target any
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,075:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: single dimension.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,075:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: It
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,075:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,085:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s worth noting that we arrived at exactly 14 signals through iterative refinement rather than upfront design. The
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,088:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: initial Phase 1 used only signals 1, 2, 10, and 11. Additional signals were added in subsequent phases as we
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,088:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: identified specific attack vectors that the existing signals couldn
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,089:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,092:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: t detect. For example, the location signals (7, 8, 9)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,093:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: were added in Phase 4 specifically to counter location spoofing attacks that we observed during Phase 3 simulations.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,094:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 43 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,095:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3.6 Algorithms Used
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,096:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: This section presents the key algorithms implemented in the NCPS, formatted in pseudocode with input/output
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,096:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: specifications.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,097:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Algorithm 1: User State Computation
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,097:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Algorithm 1: Compute User State
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,098:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ─────────────────────────────────
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,111:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Input:  user_id, vote_history[], graph_data, location_data
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,111:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Output: weight w, all intermediate scores
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,112:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1. Fetch α, β from database for user_id
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,112:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2. R ← α / (α + β)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,113:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3. Conf ← 1 - exp(-k × (α + β))        // k = 0.1
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,113:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 4. R* ← R × Conf
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,114:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 5. E ← count(vote_history)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,114:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 6. Exp ← log(1 + E) / log(1 + E_max)   // E_max = 100
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,115:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 7. S_burst ← ComputeBurstScore(vote_history)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,116:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 8. S_entropy ← ComputeEntropyScore(vote_history)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,116:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 9. S_consensus ← ComputeConsensusDeviation(vote_history)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,117:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 10. S_coord ← ComputeCoordinationScore(graph_data, user_id)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,118:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 11. S_location ← ComputeLocationAnomaly(location_data)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,118:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 12. Anom ← mean(S_burst, S_entropy, S_consensus, S_coord, S_location)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,119:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 13. T ← GetGraphTrust(user_id)           // or R* if graph not
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,120:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: enabled
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,120:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 14. w ← T × (1 - Anom) × Exp
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,121:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 15. Return w, R, R*, Conf, Exp, Anom, T
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,121:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Algorithm 2: Post Credibility Estimation
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,122:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Algorithm 2: Compute Post Credibility
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,122:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ──────────────────────────────────────
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,123:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Input:  post_id, votes[] with (user_id, value, timestamp, weight)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,123:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Output: C_final, C_Bayes, Var, N
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,123:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1. S_plus ← 0, S_minus ← 0
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,124:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2. For each vote (user_id, v, t, w) in votes:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,124:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3.     d ← exp(-λ_decay × (now - t))    // temporal decay
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,125:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 4.     prox ← ComputeProximity(user_location, post_location)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,125:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 5.     effective_w ← w × d × prox
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,125:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 6.     If v = +1: S_plus ← S_plus + effective_w
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,126:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 7.     Else:      S_minus ← S_minus + effective_w
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,126:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 8. N ← S_plus + S_minus
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,127:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 9. C_Bayes ← (α₀ + S_plus) / (α₀ + β₀ + N)   // α₀=β₀=1
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,127:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 10. Var ← Σ effective_w × (v - C_Bayes)² / N
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,128:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 11. C_ML ← MLEngine.predict(post_features)       // if Phase ≥ 5
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,128:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 12. C_memory ← MemoryEngine.score(post_content)   // if Phase ≥ 5
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,128:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 13. C_final ← 0.75 × C_Bayes + 0.15 × C_ML + 0.10 × C_memory
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,129:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 14. Return C_final, C_Bayes, Var, N
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,130:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 44 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,131:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Algorithm 3: Graph Trust Propagation
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,131:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Algorithm 3: Propagate Trust Through User Graph
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,131:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ────────────────────────────────────────────────
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,132:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Input:  adjacency_matrix A, effective_reliabilities R*, 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,132:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:         damping λ, max_iterations, tolerance ε
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,133:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Output: trust_vector T
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,133:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1. Detect coordinated clusters in A
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,134:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2. For each edge (i,j) within a coordinated cluster:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,134:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3.     A[i][j] ← A[i][j] × link_dampen_factor    // 0.1
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,135:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 4. A_norm ← row_normalize(A)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,135:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 5. T ← R*                                        // initialize
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,135:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 6. For k = 1 to max_iterations:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,136:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 7.     T_new ← λ × A_norm × T + (1 - λ) × R*
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,136:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 8.     If ||T_new - T|| < ε: break              // converged
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,137:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 9.     T ← T_new
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,137:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 10. // Apply safety constraint
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,138:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 11. For each user i:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,138:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 12.    T[i] ← min(T[i], R*[i])                  // never inflate
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,139:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 13. Return T
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,139:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Algorithm 4: Coordination Detection
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,140:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Algorithm 4: Detect Coordinated User Clusters
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,140:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ─────────────────────────────────────────────
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,140:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Input:  user_interactions[], time_threshold, agreement_threshold
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,141:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Output: coordinated_pairs[]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,141:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1. coordinated_pairs ← empty list
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,142:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2. For each pair (i, j) of users with shared posts:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,142:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3.     shared_posts ← posts voted on by both i and j
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,143:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 4.     agreement ← fraction of shared_posts where v_i = v_j
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,144:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 5.     time_sync ← fraction of shared_posts where |t_i - t_j| <
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,144:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: time_threshold
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,144:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 6.     freq ← |shared_posts| / max_possible_shared
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,145:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 7.     coord_score ← (agreement + time_sync + freq) / 3
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,145:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 8.     If coord_score > coord_threshold:           // 0.7
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,145:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 9.         coordinated_pairs.append((i, j, coord_score))
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,146:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 10. Return coordinated_pairs
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,146:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 45 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,147:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Algorithm 5: Anomaly Score Computation
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,148:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Algorithm 5: Compute Multi-Signal Anomaly Score
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,148:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ────────────────────────────────────────────────
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,149:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Input:  user_id, action_log[], graph_neighbors[],
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,149:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: location_history[]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,149:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Output: anomaly_score, sub_scores[]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,150:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1. // Burst Detection
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,150:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2. recent ← actions in last burst_window_seconds      // 60s
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,151:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3. S_burst ← min(1.0, |recent| / max_actions_per_window)  // 10
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,151:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 4. // Entropy Analysis
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,152:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 5. vote_dist ← histogram of vote values
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,152:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 6. H ← -Σ p_v × log₂(p_v)                            // Shannon entropy
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,153:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 7. S_entropy ← 1 - H / log₂(3)                        // normalized,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,153:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: inverted
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,154:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 8. // Consensus Deviation
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,154:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 9. deviations ← 0
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,154:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 10. For each voted post:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,155:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 11.    If user_vote ≠ sign(consensus): deviations++
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,155:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 12. S_consensus ← deviations / total_votes
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,156:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 13. // Coordination (from Graph Engine)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,156:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 14. S_coord ← max coordination score with any neighbor
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,157:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 15. // Location Anomaly
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,157:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 16. teleport_score ← detect_impossible_movements(location_history)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,158:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 17. device_score ← max(0, 1 - device_count / max_devices)  //
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,158:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: max_devices=5
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,159:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 18. ip_score ← max(0, 1 - ip_count / max_ips)              //
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,159:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: max_ips=10
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,160:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 19. S_location ← mean(teleport_score, 1-device_score, 1-ip_score)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,161:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 20. anomaly_score ← mean(S_burst, S_entropy, S_consensus, S_coord,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,161:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: S_location)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,162:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 21. Return anomaly_score, [S_burst, S_entropy, S_consensus,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,162:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: S_coord, S_location]
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,163:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Algorithm 6: Spatial Trust Computation
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,163:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Algorithm 6: Compute Spatial Trust and Propagation Decision
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,164:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,164:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Input:  post, voters[], thresholds
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,164:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Output: propagation_decision, new_radius
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,165:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 1. L_mean ← mean(location_confidence for each voter)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,165:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 2. 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,165:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3. // 5-Condition AND Gate
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,166:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 4. cond1 ← post.C_final ≥ 0.6
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,166:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 5. cond2 ← post.N ≥ 3.0
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,166:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 6. cond3 ← post.Var ≤ 0.25
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,167:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 7. cond4 ← (now - post.created_at) ≥ 60 seconds
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,167:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 8. cond5 ← L_mean ≥ 0.3
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,167:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 9. 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,168:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 10. If cond1 AND cond2 AND cond3 AND cond4 AND cond5:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,168:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 11.    step ← get_expansion_rate(post.C_final)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,168:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 12.    new_radius ← min(post.radius + step, max_radius)
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,169:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 13.    Return EXPAND, new_radius
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,169:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 14. Else:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,169:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 15.    Return HOLD, post.radius
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,170:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 47 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,171:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3.7 System Phases
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,177:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The NCPS was developed iteratively through six distinct phases, each adding new capabilities while preserving
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,178:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: backward compatibility with earlier features. This phased approach allowed us to measure the incremental
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,179:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: contribution of each component.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,179:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Table 3.2: System Development Phases
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,180:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Phase | Name | Components Added | Key Capability |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,180:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,181:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: |-------|------|-----------------|----------------|
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,181:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,182:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Phase 1 | Base
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,182:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Bayesian | User Engine (R, R
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,183:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: *
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,183:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ), Post Engine (C
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,183:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,184:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Bayes) | Basic credibility estimation with confidence-corrected
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,185:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: weights |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,185:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,186:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Phase 2 | Testing Infrastructure | Unit tests, integration tests | Quality assurance framework (no algorithm
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,186:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: changes) |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,187:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,188:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Phase 3 | Graph Trust | Graph Engine (coordination detection, trust propagation) | Network-aware trust
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,189:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: with coordination resistance |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,189:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,191:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Phase 4 | Spatial Trust | Spatial Engine (location confidence, proximity, propagation
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,192:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: control) | Geographic awareness and anomaly detection expansion |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,193:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,194:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Phase 5 | ML Augmentation | ML Engine
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,195:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: (LogisticRegression, TF-IDF memory) | Learning from historical patterns |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,195:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,197:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Phase 6 | Extended Signals | Signal
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,198:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Engine (burst, entropy, consensus), enhanced anomaly | Comprehensive behavioral profiling |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,200:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Each phase was validated using the same simulation framework with identical user populations and attack scenarios,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,201:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: enabling direct comparison of metrics across phases.
