   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,350:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | 
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,350:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Bot Behavior
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,350:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  | | |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,351:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,352:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Voting Pattern |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,353:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: +1 on false, -1 on true | Systematically promote false content |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,353:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,354:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Timing Jitter | 0-5 seconds | Within-group temporal
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,355:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: synchronization |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,355:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,356:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Location Spoofing | Teleport between cities | Inconsistent geographic presence |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,356:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,357:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Device Count |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,358:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 3-8 per bot | Unusual device fingerprint count |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,358:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,359:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | IP Count | 5-15 per bot | High IP address diversity |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,367:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The simulation generates realistic interaction patterns where honest users vote according to their reliability
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,370:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: probabilities (e.g., a user with p=0.85 votes correctly 85% of the time), while bots and adversarial users attempt to
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,371:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: manipulate credibility scores through coordinated false voting.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,371:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 4.3 Phase-wise Experimental Evaluation
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,372:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The following table presents the complete results across all six development phases:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,373:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Table 4.2: Phase-wise Evaluation Metric Results
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,373:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Metric | Phase 1 | Phase 3 | Phase 4 | Phase 5 | Phase 6 |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,374:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,374:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: |--------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,375:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,375:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Accuracy |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,376:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 0.900 | 0.920 | 0.920 | 1.000 | 1.000 |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,376:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,377:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Attack Success Rate (↓) | 0.150 | 0.150 | 0.150 | 0.000 | 0.000 |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,377:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,378:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Brier Score (↓) |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,378:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 0.212 | 0.221 | 0.221 | 0.153 | 0.153 |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,378:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,379:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Weight Correlation | 0.332 | 0.410 | 0.410 | 0.420 | 0.470 |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,379:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,380:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Anomaly Precision
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,380:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | 0.000 | 1.000 | 1.000 | 1.000 | 1.000 |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,381:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,381:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Anomaly Recall | 0.000 | 0.480 | 0.680 | 0.800 | 0.840 |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,382:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Note: Phase 2 is omitted as it introduced only testing infrastructure with no algorithmic changes.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,383:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 54 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,383:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The following figure provides a visual comparison of the key metrics across phases:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,385:      pdf_renderer.py:  235: /Users/chandraprakash/.gemini/antigravity/brain/608c58f2-8d2c-4b04-972b-ca1c9279e9d7/fig_5_1_phase_comparison_charts_1780257781314.png, 1024, 1024
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,391:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Fig 4.1: Phase-wise Performance Comparison showing four key metrics — Accuracy, Attack Success Rate, Anomaly
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,392:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Recall, and Weight Correlation — across Phases 1, 3, 4, 5, and 6
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,392:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Phase 1 → Phase 3: Adding Graph Trust
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,414:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Phase 1 established the baseline with pure Bayesian estimation. With 40 honest users against 25 malicious users (5
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,421:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: adversarial + 20 bots), the base system achieved a respectable 0.900 accuracy. However, the attack success rate of
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,422:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 0.150 means that 3 out of 20 false posts were incorrectly classified as credible — a dangerous outcome in a real-world
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,423:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: scenario.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,448:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The introduction of graph trust in Phase 3 improved accuracy to 0.920 and crucially introduced anomaly detection
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,462:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: capability (from 0 to 0.480 recall). The coordination detection module identified the four bot groups, dampened their
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,468:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: inter-group trust links, and propagated the distrust signal through the network. This is visible in the jump in weight
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,469:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: correlation from 0.332 to 0.410 — the system became significantly better at distinguishing trustworthy from
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,469:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: untrustworthy users.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,486:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Interestingly, the attack success rate remained at 0.150 in Phase 3. This was initially surprising to us, but upon
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,494:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: investigation we realized that the three false posts that escaped detection were supported primarily by adversarial
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,496:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: users (not bots), and the adversarial users were not coordinated — they operated independently, making them harder to
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,496:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: detect through graph-based methods alone.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,497:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Phase 3 → Phase 4: Adding Spatial Trust
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,518:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Phase 4 introduced the spatial engine, adding location-based signals and propagation control. While the headline
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,529:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: metrics (accuracy, attack success) did not change, the anomaly recall improved dramatically from 0.480 to 0.680.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,533:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: This is because the spatial engine caught bots that the graph engine missed — specifically, bots exhibiting location
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,534:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: spoofing (teleporting between cities) and using suspicously many devices and IP addresses.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,540:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The combination of graph-based and spatial-based anomaly signals proved complementary. Some bots that managed
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,541:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: to avoid coordination detection (perhaps by adding randomized delays to their voting patterns) were caught by the
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,541:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: spatial engine
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,542:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,545:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s device fingerprinting. This is exactly why we designed the system to use multiple independent
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,546:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: signals — its much harder for an attacker to simultaneously evade all detection dimensions.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,547:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 56 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,548:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Phase 4 → Phase 5: Adding ML Augmentation
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,564:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Phase 5 introduced machine learning augmentation and the memory module, and this produced the most dramatic
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,571:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: improvement in the results. Accuracy jumped from 0.920 to a perfect 1.000, and the attack success rate dropped to
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,572:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 0.000. This means that every single post — true or false — was correctly classified, and not a single false post escaped
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,573:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: detection.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,601:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The ML component was able to learn the subtle patterns that distinguished true from false posts beyond what pure
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,618:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Bayesian estimation could capture. The LogisticRegression model identified that false posts tend to have higher
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,627:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: variance-to-evidence ratios, higher concentrations of anomalous voters, and different temporal spread patterns
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,630:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: compared to true posts. Even for the three false posts that had escaped detection in earlier phases, the ML
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,631:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: component pushed their credibility scores below the 0.5 threshold.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,631:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The Brier score also improved significantly, from 0.221 to 0.153. This indicates better calibration — the system
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,632:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,637:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,641:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: confidence levels more accurately reflect the actual probability of posts being true. Anomaly recall continued to
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,641:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: improve to 0.800, meaning the system now catches 80% of all malicious users.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,642:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Phase 5 → Phase 6: Extended Signals
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,655:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Phase 6 added three new behavioral signals (burst detection, entropy analysis, and consensus deviation) to the
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,661:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: anomaly computation. While the headline accuracy and attack success rate remained at their perfect levels (1.000
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,663:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: and 0.000 respectively), the weight correlation improved from 0.420 to 0.470, and anomaly recall increased from
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,663:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 0.800 to 0.840.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,664:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The improvement in weight correlation is particularly noteworthy because it means the system
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,664:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,664:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s user weight
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,665:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: estimates are increasingly aligned with users
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,665:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,683:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  true reliabilities. The three new behavioral signals provided additional
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,695:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: dimensions for distinguishing honest from malicious users, particularly for the remaining undetected adversarial
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,700:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: users who managed to avoid both graph and spatial detection. The burst detection caught users with unnatural voting
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,701:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: cadences, and the consensus deviation signal identified users who consistently voted against the emerging
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,701:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: consensus.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,702:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 57 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,703:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 4.4 Frontend Implementation Screenshots
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,705:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The NCPS is implemented as a full-stack web application with a modern, dark-themed user interface. This section
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,706:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: presents screenshots of the key pages and their functionality.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,706:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 4.4.1 Login and Authentication Interface
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,708:      pdf_renderer.py:  235: /Users/chandraprakash/.gemini/antigravity/brain/608c58f2-8d2c-4b04-972b-ca1c9279e9d7/fig_4_4_login_page_1780257675874.png, 1024, 1024
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,711:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Fig 4.2: Login and Authentication Interface of the NCPS web application
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,754:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Fig 4.2 shows the login page of the NCPS web application. The interface features a dark-themed design with
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,782:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: glassmorphism effects on the login card. Users can enter their email address and password to authenticate, or
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,798:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: navigate to the registration page to create a new account. Authentication is handled via JWT tokens — upon successful
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,804:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: login, the server issues a token that is stored client-side and included in subsequent API requests. The navigation bar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,804:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: at the top provides links to the Home, Map, and Insights pages, though these are accessible only after authentication.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,805:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 4.4.2 Home Feed with Credibility-Ranked Reports
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,806:      pdf_renderer.py:  235: /Users/chandraprakash/.gemini/antigravity/brain/608c58f2-8d2c-4b04-972b-ca1c9279e9d7/fig_4_5_home_feed_1780257695514.png, 1024, 1024
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,810:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Fig 4.3: Home Feed showing news reports with credibility scores, urgency badges, location tags, and voting buttons
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,862:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The home feed page (Fig 4.3) is the primary interface for viewing and interacting with local news reports. Each
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,898:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: report card displays the report title, content preview, credibility score with a color-coded progress bar (green for
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,919:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: high credibility, yellow for medium, red for low), urgency badge, location tag, upvote and downvote buttons with
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,929:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: counts, and timestamp. Users can filter reports by category (Latest, Popular, Urgent, My Reports) and search for
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,933:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: specific topics. The sidebar displays trending categories and top contributors, providing community context. The
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,933:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: credibility bar is the most distinctive element — it immediately communicates the system
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,934:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,934:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s assessment of each report
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,934:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,935:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,935:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: reliability to the reader.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,936:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 59 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,937:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 4.4.3 Interactive Map with Propagation Radius
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,937:      pdf_renderer.py:  235: /Users/chandraprakash/.gemini/antigravity/brain/608c58f2-8d2c-4b04-972b-ca1c9279e9d7/fig_4_6_map_page_1780257710613.png, 1024, 1024
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,943:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Fig 4.4: Interactive Leaflet.js map showing post locations with credibility-colored markers, user locations (blue
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:58,944:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: dots), propagation radius circles, and nearby reports sidebar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,047:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Fig 4.4 presents the map page, which provides a geographic visualization of all reports and users. Built on Leaflet.js
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,123:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: with OpenStreetMap tiles, the map displays several types of markers: green markers for high-credibility posts, red
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,177:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: markers for low-credibility posts, and blue dots for user locations. Each post marker is surrounded by a translucent
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,211:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: circle representing its current propagation radius — larger circles indicate posts that have expanded their reach due to
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,231:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: meeting the 5-condition propagation gate. Clicking on a marker shows a popup with the post title and credibility
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,242:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: score. The sidebar panel lists nearby reports with their credibility assessments, allowing users to quickly scan reports
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,245:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: relevant to their location. This spatial visualization is unique to the NCPS — no other fact-checking system we are
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,245:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: aware of provides this kind of geographic credibility view.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,246:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 4.4.4 User Profile with Trust Signal Decomposition
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,247:      pdf_renderer.py:  235: /Users/chandraprakash/.gemini/antigravity/brain/608c58f2-8d2c-4b04-972b-ca1c9279e9d7/fig_4_7_profile_trust_1780257834705.png, 1024, 1024
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,251:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Fig 4.5: User profile page showing trust signal bars for Reliability, Experience, Anomaly, Trust, and Location
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,252:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Confidence, along with the weight decomposition formula
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,255:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The profile page (Fig 4.5) provides users with complete transparency into how their trust score is computed. Five
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,255:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: horizontal progress bars display the individual trust signals: Reliability (R
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,256:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: *
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,295:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: ), Experience, Anomaly Score, Graph
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,328:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Trust, and Location Confidence. Below these bars, the weight decomposition formula shows exactly how these
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,349:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: signals combine to produce the final weight. For example, a user with Trust=0.81, Anomaly=0.05, and
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,360:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Experience=0.72 would have a weight of 0.81 × 0.95 × 0.72 = 0.554. This transparency is a deliberate design choice —
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,363:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: we believe that users should understand why their votes carry a particular weight, and seeing the decomposition
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,364:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: encourages behaviors that build trust (consistent voting, stable location, active participation).
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,365:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 61 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,365:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 4.4.5 Simulation Dashboard
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,367:      pdf_renderer.py:  235: /Users/chandraprakash/.gemini/antigravity/brain/608c58f2-8d2c-4b04-972b-ca1c9279e9d7/fig_4_8_simulation_dashboard_1780257767552.png, 1024, 1024
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,375:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Fig 4.6: Simulation dashboard showing phase selector, metric cards (Accuracy, Attack Success, Brier Score, Weight
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,376:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Correlation), color-coded user table, D3.js force-directed network graph, and post credibility list
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,419:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The simulation dashboard (Fig 4.6) provides a comprehensive view of system performance during simulation runs.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,447:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The top row contains phase selector buttons and summary metric cards. The middle section displays a color-coded
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,462:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: user table (green for honest, red for bots, yellow for adversarial) with columns for all computed scores, alongside an
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,470:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: interactive D3.js force-directed network graph that visualizes the user interaction graph. Coordinated bot clusters are
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,472:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: visually apparent as tightly connected red node groups. The bottom section shows a post credibility list with
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,472:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: horizontal bars indicating each post
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,472:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,474:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s final credibility score. This dashboard was invaluable during development — it
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,474:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: allowed us to visually inspect the system
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,475:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,476:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s behavior and quickly identify issues like insufficient coordination
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,477:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: detection or overly aggressive anomaly scoring.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,477:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 4.5 Functional Testing
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,480:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Beyond simulation-based evaluation, we conducted comprehensive functional testing of all system components. The
