   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,514:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 4.6 Stress Test Results
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,516:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: To evaluate system robustness under extreme conditions, we conducted three stress test scenarios that push the
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,517:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: system well beyond normal operating parameters:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,517:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Table 4.4: Stress Test Scenarios and Results
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,518:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Scenario | Configuration | Accuracy | Attack Success |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,518:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,519:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: |----------|--------------|----------|---------------|
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,519:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,521:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Adversarial
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,522:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Majority | 64% adversarial users (45 out of 70) | 1.000 | 0.000 |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,522:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,523:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Bot Swarm | 50% bots (35 out of 70) in 7
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,524:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: coordinated groups | 1.000 | 0.000 |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,524:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment:  
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,525:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: | Low Activity | Only 60 interactions (avg ~1.2 per post) | 1.000 | 0.000 |
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,544:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: These results are quite remarkable. Even when adversarial users constitute a clear majority (64%), the system
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,554:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: maintains perfect accuracy. This is because the Bayesian confidence correction ensures that the large number of
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,557:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: adversarial accounts — which are typically new or have inconsistent track records — carry very low weights. Their
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,558:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: numerical advantage is neutralized by their individually low influence.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,568:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The bot swarm scenario is similarly robust. Even with 35 bots organized in 7 coordinated groups (each group of 5
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,571:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: bots acting in concert), the coordination detection module identifies and dampens the bot clusters, and the trust
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,572:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: propagation ensures that distrust flows through the entire bot network.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,589:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The low activity scenario tests the system under data-sparse conditions. With only 60 total interactions across 50
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,597:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: posts, each post has barely more than one vote on average. Despite this extreme sparsity, the system maintains
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,599:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: perfect accuracy, largely due to the conservative priors (starting at 0.5) which prevent the system from making
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,599:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: confident wrong assessments when evidence is scarce.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,600:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 4.7 Discussion
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,600:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: The experimental results demonstrate several important properties of the NCPS architecture:
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,601:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Progressive Improvement
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,611:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : Each phase contributed measurable improvements to at least one metric, validating the
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,616:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: modular, phased development approach. The most significant improvements came from ML augmentation (Phase
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,617:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 5), which closed the remaining accuracy gap, and graph trust (Phase 3), which introduced coordination detection
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,617:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: capabilities.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,618:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Multi-Signal Robustness
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,618:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : The system
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,618:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: '
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,633:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: s resilience against diverse attack types arises from the multiplicative
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,642:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: combination of independent signals. An attacker must simultaneously evade Bayesian reliability tracking, graph
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,647:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: coordination detection, spatial anomaly detection, behavioral analysis, AND ML-based pattern recognition.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,647:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Compromising any single dimension is insufficient because the remaining dimensions still expose the attack.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,648:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Conservative Design
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,648:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : The safety constraint (T
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,648:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,649:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i ≤ R
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,649:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: *
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,649:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: _
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,663:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: i) and the 5-condition propagation gate ensure that the system
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,671:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: errs on the side of caution. In practice, this means some true posts may experience slightly delayed propagation, but
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,672:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: no false posts gain wide distribution — a trade-off that we believe is appropriate for a system designed to protect
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,672:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: communities from misinformation.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,673:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: Limitations
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,691:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: : The system is validated through simulation only. Real-world user behavior may differ from simulated
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,701:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: patterns in ways that affect performance. Additionally, the current implementation does not analyze content (text,
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,705:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: images) for signs of fabrication, relying entirely on network-level signals. Integration of content analysis could
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,705:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: further improve performance, particularly for cases where the social signal is ambiguous.
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,706:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: 65 — Department of Computer Science and Engineering, National Institute of Technology Srinagar
   DEBUG: 2026-06-01 02:19:59,707:      pdf_renderer.py:  470: printSegment: <div style="page-break-after: always;"></div>
